Training examples peak on 'data', but weaken in storage/read-write contexts.
The spelling and attached code punctuation set the main response. Several
translations of data also respond. A preceding storage/IO term reduces the
response, while an owner or determiner increases it slightly. Payload words
such as file or format get a negative response immediately after IO terms.
Otherwise predict zero. Context is one token, within the same document.
